                    <death when="1840"/>
                    <occupation>Philologist and Schoolmaster</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>2In 1794 Godwin reads 'An Essay on
                            Philosophical Necessity' by Alexander Crombie. The later Crombie entries - 2.11.1809 write to,
                            29.12.1809 at Joseph Johnson's funeral, 28.1.1810 write to, 24.1.1811
                            calls, 25.1.1811 at Joseph (jr) Johnson's, 17.4.1811 adv at theatre,
                            21.12.1826 adv at Museum - probably all referred to the author of that
                            text, Rev Alexander Crombie DNB 1760-1840, Doctor of Laws, who kept an
                            academy at Newington Green 1792 with Rev James Lindsay and at Highgate
                            1795, in 1823 was late of Greenwich, now of Cadogan Pl, Sloane St,
                            elected FRS 1829, will PCC 1840 of St Marylebone </p>
                    </note>
